### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### INTERACTIONS — Inquiry / Complaint / Feedback
### (InteractionType:  0 = Inquiry  |  1 = Complaint  |  2 = Feedback)
### (Status:           0 = Open     |  1 = InProgress |  2 = Closed)
### (Priority:         0 = Low      |  1 = Medium     |  2 = High)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 21. CREATE Inquiry
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "interactionType": 0,
  "priority": 1,
  "subject": "Warranty question",
  "notes": "Customer asking if laptop is still under warranty.",
  "interactionByUserId": "staff-001"
}

### 22. CREATE Complaint
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "interactionType": 1,
  "priority": 2,
  "subject": "Slow repair turnaround",
  "notes": "Customer unhappy with the delay on repair request REQ-001.",
  "interactionByUserId": "staff-001"
}

### 23. CREATE Feedback
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "interactionType": 2,
  "priority": 0,
  "subject": "Great service",
  "notes": "Customer said the technician was very helpful.",
  "interactionByUserId": "staff-001"
}

### 24. READ all active interactions
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions
Accept: application/json

### 25. READ only Inquiries (type=0)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions?type=0
Accept: application/json

### 26. READ only Complaints (type=1)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions?type=1
Accept: application/json

### 27. READ only Feedback (type=2)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions?type=2
Accept: application/json

### 28. READ one interaction (id 1)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions/1
Accept: application/json

### 29. UPDATE interaction 1 — mark InProgress (status=1)
PUT {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "interactionType": 0,
  "status": 1,
  "priority": 1,
  "subject": "Warranty question (in progress)",
  "notes": "Updated notes while investigating.",
  "resolution": null
}

### 30. UPDATE interaction 1 — mark Closed (status=2) with resolution
PUT {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "interactionType": 0,
  "status": 2,
  "priority": 1,
  "subject": "Warranty question (closed)",
  "notes": "Updated notes while investigating.",
  "resolution": "Confirmed warranty covered for 12 more months."
}

### 31. ARCHIVE interaction 1 (soft delete)
DELETE {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions/1

### 32. READ all INCLUDING archived
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions?includeArchived=true
Accept: application/json

### 33. RESTORE interaction 1
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions/1/restore

### 34. CONFIRM restore (should be active again)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/interactions/1
Accept: application/json

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### FOLLOW-UPS — Full CRUD
### (Status:  0 = Scheduled | 1 = Completed | 2 = Cancelled)
### (Channel: 0 = Call      | 1 = Email     | 2 = SMS       | 3 = Visit)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 40. CREATE Follow-Up (Call)
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "subject": "Call about repair pickup",
  "notes": "Remind customer that device is ready.",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-09-20T10:00:00",
  "channel": 0,
  "status": 0,
  "assignedToUserId": "staff-001"
}

### 41. CREATE Follow-Up (Email)
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "subject": "Send invoice email",
  "notes": "Email the final invoice.",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-09-21T09:00:00",
  "channel": 1,
  "status": 0,
  "assignedToUserId": "staff-001"
}

### 42. READ all active follow-ups
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups
Accept: application/json

### 43. READ only Scheduled (status=0)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups?status=0
Accept: application/json

### 44. READ only Completed (status=1)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups?status=1
Accept: application/json

### 45. READ one follow-up (id 1)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups/1
Accept: application/json

### 46. UPDATE follow-up 1 — mark Completed (status=1)
PUT {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": null,
  "repairRequestId": null,
  "subject": "Call about repair pickup (done)",
  "notes": "Called customer, will pick up Friday.",
  "scheduledAt": "2026-09-20T10:00:00",
  "channel": 0,
  "status": 1,
  "assignedToUserId": "staff-001"
}

### 47. ARCHIVE follow-up 1 (soft delete)
DELETE {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups/1

### 48. READ all INCLUDING archived
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups?includeArchived=true
Accept: application/json

### 49. RESTORE follow-up 1
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/follow-ups/1/restore

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### REPAIR REQUESTS — Full CRUD with status workflow
### (Status:   0 = Pending | 1 = Approved | 2 = InProgress
###            3 = Completed | 4 = Rejected | 5 = Reassigned)
### (Priority: 0 = Low | 1 = Medium | 2 = High | 3 = Urgent)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### 60. CREATE Repair Request
POST {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/repair-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "deviceId": null,
  "deviceModel": "Dell Latitude 5420",
  "serialNumber": "SN-ABC123",
  "issueDescription": "Laptop won't boot past BIOS screen.",
  "priority": 2,
  "estimatedCost": 1500.00
}

### 61. READ all repair requests
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/repair-requests
Accept: application/json

### 62. READ only Pending (status=0)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/repair-requests?status=0
Accept: application/json

### 63. READ one repair request (id 1)
GET {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/repair-requests/1
Accept: application/json

### 64. UPDATE repair request 1 — Approved (status=1)
PUT {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/repair-requests/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "deviceId": null,
  "deviceModel": "Dell Latitude 5420",
  "serialNumber": "SN-ABC123",
  "issueDescription": "Laptop won't boot past BIOS screen.",
  "status": 1,
  "priority": 2,
  "estimatedCost": 1500.00,
  "technicianNotes": "Approved for repair.",
  "assignedToStaffId": "staff-001"
}

### 65. UPDATE repair request 1 — Completed (status=3)
PUT {{CRM_ComputerRepair.api_HostAddress}}/tenant/1/repair-requests/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1,
  "deviceId": null,
  "deviceModel": "Dell Latitude 5420",
  "serialNumber": "SN-ABC123",
  "issueDescription": "Laptop won't boot past BIOS screen.",
  "status": 3,
  "priority": 2,
  "estimatedCost": 1500.00,
  "actualCost": 1400.00,
  "technicianNotes": "Replaced SSD. Working now.",
  "assignedToStaffId": "staff-001"
}